Z||000000||fiero56||02-05-2000||12:19 PM||||Just got done with the soutwestern Ohio trip. 5 people showed up. What a blast! Got to meet Monkeyman, in person. What a funny guy.<BR>The day was sunny and in the lower 30s. Snow on the ground, with salted roads and little patches of ice. <BR>Had a good breakfast at Cracker Barrel, filled up at BP, then headed out. There were a few VERY steep hills with some tricky curves, but we all made it through. No one got stuck, and no skids off the road. Was a good time.<BR>People who showed up: BENGAL4, M-Man, William Thorn III, Scott2m4, and I. Whens the next one?||||reg||10
Z||000001||Scott2M4||02-06-2000||05:52 PM||||<B>I</B>.....<B>HAD</B>.....<B>A</B>.....<B>BLAST!!!!!</B><P>Great to have all of you there.  It was a pleasure!  Monkeyman, are you planning to post any of the pics?<P>Next one may be on 2/26 with Columbus folks - ChadMan, maybe others.  I'll keep you posted.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-06-2000||06:07 PM||||<B>I HAVEN'T HAD THAT MUCH FUN IN A LONG TIME!!!!</B><BR>What a blast!  Although I wasn't able to drive my own Fiero, I got to ride with WT III.  Only one close call that I can remember.  I have to remember not to talk about stereos with the driver when everyone else decides to stop/turn!!  No problem, though.  I was thrilled to meet Scott2m4 and fiero56 (I had already met the others--Nice to see them again, though.).  I really enjoy meeting fellow Fieroholics.  It's good to be able to put a name with a face.  Here's a pic of everyone but me.  (I'll do something with the rest of them later.  I just got home.)  I wasn't in the pic because I still can't figure out how to use the timer on the camera (and because of that nasty Witness Relocation Program thing!).<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Ohio_trip1.JPG"> <BR>The pic sucks, but I thought it would turn out better.  Starting on the left:  William Thorn III ('85GT), fiero56 ('88 Formula), Scott2m4 ('87 coupe), and BENGAL4 ('86GT).  If we'd had an '84 and a pre-'87 coupe, we would have had every year and body style accounted for.  I have some other pics, but it'll take me a little while to get them off of my camera.  Look for them later!||||reg||1
Z||000003||BENGAL4||02-06-2000||08:15 PM||||Thanks Scott for getting this together. It was great to meet everyone. I think it's cool that people of different ages, occupations and other interests, can meet and share the one thing they have in common. BTW, Monkey is just as funny in person as he is on the Forum. But if you seen him, you would know why he isn't in the pic.   ||||reg||6
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-07-2000||05:57 AM||||Yup.  I'm big and goofy looking.  I'd hate to break a $200 camera.||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||02-07-2000||11:58 AM||||Monkey,<P>I was thinking that we should have taken another picture of you in front of my 85 since you will be getting one of your own soon!  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000006||Monkeyman||02-07-2000||08:26 PM||||Good idea.  Too bad we didn't think of it while we were there.  Maybe I'll be able to get mine before I get too old to drive it.  Might call the guy tomorrow since he won't answer my emails.||||reg||1
